            "finalAnswer": "I have enough to give a complete trace.\n\n## Trace\n\n**1. React component → `renderStaticScene`**\n\n`StaticCanvas` (`packages/excalidraw/components/canvases/StaticCanvas.tsx:68`) is the React component that invokes `renderStaticScene()` from `renderer/staticScene.ts`, inside a `useEffect` that fires on every render (so it re-runs any time relevant props change, per the `React.memo`/`areEqual` comparator at the bottom of the file). It's a \"headless\" component — it renders just a wrapper `<div>` and does all real drawing imperatively via the effect.\n\n**2. `renderStaticScene` → `renderElement`**\n\n`renderStaticScene` (optionally throttled to `requestAnimationFrame` via `renderStaticSceneThrottled`) iterates `visibleElements` and calls `renderElement(element, elementsMap, allElementsMap, rc, context, renderConfig, appState)` for each one (`renderer/staticScene.ts:314-345` etc.), where `rc` is the `RoughCanvas` instance passed down from `StaticCanvas`'s props (itself created in `scene/Renderer.ts`/App).\n\n**3. `renderElement` → `drawElementOnCanvas` → `ShapeCache`**\n\n`renderElement` (in `renderer/renderElement.ts`) first ensures a rough.js shape exists by calling `ShapeCache.generateElementShape(element, renderConfig)` (line ~811), then calls `drawElementOnCanvas`, which does the actual drawing:\n\n```ts\ncase \"rectangle\": case \"diamond\": case \"ellipse\": ...\n  rc.draw(ShapeCache.get(element)!);\n```\n\n**4. Where the roughjs shape comes from — `ShapeCache` (`scene/ShapeCache.ts`)**\n\n`ShapeCache` is a `WeakMap<ExcalidrawElement, ElementShape>` keyed on the element object itself. `ShapeCache.generateElementShape`:\n- Returns the cached shape if one already exists (and we're not exporting).\n- Otherwise generates a new shape by calling `_generateElementShape(element, ShapeCache.rg, renderConfig)` from `scene/Shape.ts`, where `ShapeCache.rg` is a shared `RoughGenerator` instance (`new RoughGenerator()` from `roughjs/bin/generator`). `_generateElementShape` dispatches on `element.type` and calls the appropriate rough.js generator method (`generator.rectangle`, `generator.ellipse`, `generator.path`, `generator.curve`, etc.) to build the `Drawable`.\n- Caches the result in the WeakMap keyed by the element, so subsequent renders of an unchanged element reuse the same `Drawable` instead of regenerating it (invalidation happens via `ShapeCache.delete`/mutation elsewhere when the element's geometry/style changes).\n\nSo the flow is: `StaticCanvas` (React) → `renderStaticScene` → `renderElement`/`drawElementOnCanvas` → `ShapeCache.get`/`generateElementShape` (cache-or-generate via `roughjs`'s `RoughGenerator` in `scene/Shape.ts`) → `rc.draw(shape)` paints it onto the `CanvasRenderingContext2D`.",
